1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:07,150
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:07,150
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:15,110
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:15,110
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,790
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:26,000
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:26,000
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,800
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,800
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:37,470
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:37,550
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:44,730
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:44,730
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:52,070
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:52,070
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:55,950
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:55,950
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,870
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,870
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:03,160
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:03,160
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:06,830
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:06,960
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:10,960
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,960
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,630
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,630
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:18,470
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:18,470
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:21,970
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:21,970
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:25,730
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:25,730
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:29,770
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:29,770
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,150
REASON FOR EXISTING, RAISON D'ÊTRE

37
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:33,820
THE REASON WHY ONE IS ALLOWED TO BE HERE

38
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,570
IN THE CASE OF SHINJI IKARI

39
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,490
THE BOY WISHED FOR DEATH OF HIS OWN WILL

40
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,990
THE BOY GRANTED HIS WISH

41
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,580
THE FINAL ANGEL IS GONE

42
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,880
BUT SHINJI IKARI IS TORMENTED

43
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,380
WHY DID YOU KILL HIM?

44
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:56,010
WHY DID YOU KILL HIM?

45
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,050
WHY DID YOU KILL HIM?

46
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:01,010
WHY DID YOU KILL HIM?

47
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:05,100
WHY DID YOU KILL HIM?

48
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:07,770
Because I had no choice!

49
00:02:07,770 --> 00:02:09,100
WHY DID YOU KILL HIM?

50
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:12,110
Because Kaworu was... He was an Angel!

51
00:02:12,110 --> 00:02:13,270
EVEN THOUGH HE WAS ALSO HUMAN?

52
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:16,420
No! An Angel! He was our enemy!

53
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:17,650
EVEN THOUGH HE WAS HUMAN, LIKE YOU?

54
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:20,720
No! No! You're wrong!

55
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:23,780
Even though he was a person, just like me?

56
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:26,310
No! He was an Angel!

57
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:27,950
That's why you killed him?

58
00:02:27,950 --> 00:02:31,350
That's right! If I hadn't, we would've died!

59
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:33,020
Everyone would have been killed!

60
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,290
That's why you killed him?

61
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:36,160
I didn't do it because I wanted to!

62
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:37,920
I had no choice.

63
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:38,970
THAT'S WHY YOU KILLED HIM

64
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:40,450
Help me...

65
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:41,470
THAT'S WHY YOU KILLED HIM

66
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:42,640
Help me.

67
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,600
THAT'S WHY YOU KILLED HIM

68
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,560
Help me!

69
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,140
THAT'S WHY YOU KILLED HIM

70
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:47,640
Someone, help me!

71
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,810
THAT'S WHY YOU KILLED HIM

72
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:51,810
Please, someone just help me!

73
00:02:56,280 --> 00:03:00,520
That's right, Kaworu was the one
who should have survived.

74
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:04,370
He was a much better person than I am.

75
00:03:04,930 --> 00:03:07,490
Kaworu should have been the one to survive.

76
00:03:07,490 --> 00:03:08,620
You're wrong.

77
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:11,470
Only those who have the will
to live get to survive.

78
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,660
He wished to die.

79
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,940
He abandoned his will to live,
clinging instead to a false hope.

80
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:19,870
You did nothing wrong, Shinji.

81
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:21,050
Is that true?

82
00:03:21,090 --> 00:03:21,800
UNCERTAINTY

83
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:24,020
Is this really how it should be?

84
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:24,550
HAUNTING UNCERTAINTY

85
00:03:24,550 --> 00:03:27,740
I don't know. What should I do?

86
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,130
What am I supposed to do?!

87
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:30,180
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?

88
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:31,230
Afraid of?

89
00:03:31,270 --> 00:03:32,140
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?

90
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:33,200
Me?

91
00:03:33,230 --> 00:03:34,100
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?

92
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:35,400
Being hated.

93
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,230
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?

94
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:36,940
By whom?

95
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:37,570
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?

96
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,560
By whom?

97
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:38,780
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?

98
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:41,820
By Father!

99
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:44,500
Father abandoned me! He hated me!

100
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:47,830
What will I do if people hate me?

101
00:03:47,830 --> 00:03:49,570
What should I do?

102
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,280
Where am I?

103
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,420
Where am I supposed to go?

104
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:07,860
I can't see anything. I don't know what's what.

105
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:11,770
Miss Misato?

106
00:04:12,630 --> 00:04:14,130
Miss Misato?!

107
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:17,650
Hey, where did you go, Miss Misato?

108
00:04:18,470 --> 00:04:22,040
Hey, where am I supposed to go now?

109
00:04:22,810 --> 00:04:26,170
Miss Misato! Asuka! Ayanami!

110
00:04:26,170 --> 00:04:28,570
Toji! Kensuke! Miss Ritsuko!

111
00:04:28,570 --> 00:04:30,000
Mr. Kaji!

112
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,380
Father!

113
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:33,350
Mother...

114
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,480
Someone tell me.

115
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:38,190
Tell me what I'm supposed to do.

116
00:04:40,590 --> 00:04:42,300
Evangelion Unit 01...

117
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:48,430
So, do I ultimately have no choice
but to pilot it?

118
00:04:48,970 --> 00:04:51,360
Even after killing someone I loved?

119
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:54,090
Are you saying I'm supposed to listen
to my father and everyone else,

120
00:04:54,090 --> 00:04:56,030
and get back in this thing to fight?!

121
00:04:56,030 --> 00:04:57,460
Mother!

122
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:59,650
Say something! Answer me!

123
00:04:59,690 --> 00:05:00,900
WHY DO YOU PILOT THE EVA?

124
00:05:02,350 --> 00:05:04,020
Because everyone tells me to pilot it.

125
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:05,400
THAT'S WHY YOU PILOT THE EVA?

126
00:05:05,550 --> 00:05:09,660
It's... It's for the good of everybody,
so why does it matter?!

127
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,740
SO, YOU PILOT THE EVA FOR EVERYBODY,
FOR OTHERS?

128
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:14,590
That's right. It's a good thing!

129
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:16,750
It's a very good thing!

130
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:20,800
If I pilot it, everyone praises me!
They treat me well!

131
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,460
That's a lie!

132
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:24,260
What are you, stupid?!

133
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:26,550
In the end, you're just doing it for yourself!

134
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:30,680
And there you go, making up excuses
for yourself again!

135
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,830
I am?

136
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:36,440
Thinking that you're working hard
for the sake of others!

137
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:38,870
That in and of itself is the easy way to live!

138
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:40,320
Really?

139
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:43,660
In other words, you're lonely, Shinji.

140
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:45,180
Really?

141
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,250
That's just being dependent!

142
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:49,730
It's nothing but a symbiotic relationship!

143
00:05:49,730 --> 00:05:51,600
You might be right.

144
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:56,160
You just want people to need you!

145
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,460
You might be right.

146
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:03,400
All you do is wait, wanting people
to give you happiness!

147
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,140
False happiness!

148
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:07,550
But that goes for you too.

149
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,340
THE SECOND CHARACTER

150
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:11,680
IN THE CASE OF ASUKA LANGLEY SOHRYU

151
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:19,950
I don't remember getting on,
but I'm back in the Eva again.

152
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:21,690
I was put back in.

153
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:25,500
It's not going to move anyway, piece of junk.

154
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:30,140
No, I'm the piece of junk.

155
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:34,900
They don't need me! No one needs me!

156
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:39,880
No one needs a pilot who can't control her Eva!

157
00:06:40,610 --> 00:06:43,370
So, you're seeking to find yourself in others.

158
00:06:43,370 --> 00:06:44,170
Shut up!

159
00:06:44,210 --> 00:06:45,090
SEPARATION ANXIETY

160
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,630
You're afraid of becoming alone, aren't you?

161
00:06:47,670 --> 00:06:48,340
SEPARATION ANXIETY

162
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:52,300
Because you disappear along with the people
around you. That's why you're afraid, aren't you?

163
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:52,840
SEPARATION ANXIETY

164
00:06:53,090 --> 00:06:55,200
That's why you pilot the Eva!

165
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:55,720
ATTACHMENT BEHAVIOR

166
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,800
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

167
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,350
ATTACHMENT BEHAVIOR

168
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:01,940
I don't want to hear that from a puppet like you!

169
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:03,020
THE THIRD CHARACTER

170
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:04,610
IN THE CASE OF REI AYANAMI

171
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,790
Who am I?

172
00:07:06,790 --> 00:07:08,490
Rei Ayanami.

173
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:10,070
Who are you?

174
00:07:10,110 --> 00:07:11,570
REI AYANAMI

175
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,080
You're also Rei Ayanami?

176
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:17,550
Yes, I am the thing that is called Rei Ayanami.

177
00:07:17,550 --> 00:07:20,460
We are all things that are called Rei Ayanami.

178
00:07:20,950 --> 00:07:22,920
How can we all be me?

179
00:07:23,590 --> 00:07:27,860
Because everybody calls us Rei Ayanami.

180
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:31,830
Why do you possess a false heart and body?

181
00:07:32,130 --> 00:07:35,350
They are not false, because I am me.

182
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:42,510
No, you are a person whose false soul was
created by the human named Gendo Ikari.

183
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:47,610
You're nothing but an object living a lie,
pretending to be a person.

184
00:07:48,010 --> 00:07:50,840
See? There's a dark part
of your heart inside you

185
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:54,530
that you can see nothing of,
that you know nothing of.

186
00:07:55,150 --> 00:07:57,960
That's where the real you is.

187
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,860
I am me.

188
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:02,850
Because I became who I am
through the time I've spent

189
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:05,290
and the connections I've made
with other people.

190
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:11,040
The current me has been molded
through contact with other people.

191
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:16,180
Contact with people and the passage of time
change the shape of my heart.

192
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:17,430
"IS THAT WHAT TIES ARE?"

193
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:22,790
Yes, the things that have created the me
called Rei Ayanami so far...

194
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:25,460
The things that will continue to shape me...

195
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,770
"THAT IS WHAT TIES ARE"

196
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:30,030
But the real you is somewhere else.

197
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:32,990
You just don't know it.

198
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:35,680
Because you don't want to see it.

199
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,700
You're just avoiding it without realizing it.

200
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:38,830
"BECAUSE YOU'RE AFRAID"

201
00:08:38,870 --> 00:08:41,910
Because it may not be human in form.

202
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:45,870
Because the person that I have been
so far may cease to exist.

203
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:47,580
"YOU ARE AFRAID"

204
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:50,380
You're afraid of ceasing to exist.

205
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:54,880
You're afraid of being erased
from everyone's hearts.

206
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,440
Afraid?

207
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:57,740
I don't understand.

208
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,390
Your own individual world
will also cease to exist.

209
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:01,520
"IT FRIGHTENS YOU, DOESN'T IT?"

210
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:03,390
You will cease to exist.

211
00:09:03,430 --> 00:09:04,520
"IT FRIGHTENS YOU, DOESN'T IT?"

212
00:09:05,890 --> 00:09:08,070
No, it makes me happy.

213
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,820
Because I want to die.

214
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:12,650
What I desire is despair.

215
00:09:12,650 --> 00:09:14,290
I want to return to nothingness.

216
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:15,790
But I can't.

217
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,690
I cannot return to nothingness.

218
00:09:17,690 --> 00:09:19,470
He won't let me return.

219
00:09:20,210 --> 00:09:22,140
He won't let me go back yet.

220
00:09:22,570 --> 00:09:25,120
I existed because he needed me.

221
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:27,300
But it's over now.

222
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:29,500
He's not going to need me anymore.

223
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:31,890
He's going to abandon me.

224
00:09:32,590 --> 00:09:35,330
I thought I had wished for
that day to come, but...

225
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,520
Now, I am afraid.

226
00:09:42,430 --> 00:09:44,130
Come, let us go.

227
00:09:44,430 --> 00:09:49,100
You have existed for this day, today, Rei.

228
00:09:49,670 --> 00:09:50,380
Yes!

229
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,440
AND THEN...

230
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,440
THE INSTRUMENTALITY OF MANKIND BEGINS

231
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,860
EPISODE 25

232
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,860
THE WORLD ENDING

233
00:09:58,780 --> 00:09:59,990
ONCE AGAIN, SHINJI IKARI

234
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:03,990
What is this sensation?

235
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:07,140
I feel like I've experienced it before,

236
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:10,160
as if the shape of my body is melting away.

237
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:12,890
It feels so good.

238
00:10:13,730 --> 00:10:16,660
I feel like I'm growing, expanding outward...

239
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:19,800
On and on...

240
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:21,800
THAT WAS THE BEGINNING OF THE
INSTRUMENTALITY OF PEOPLE

241
00:10:21,850 --> 00:10:23,050
WHAT PEOPLE ARE LACKING

242
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,260
THE LOSS IN THEIR HEARTS

243
00:10:24,310 --> 00:10:25,600
IN ORDER TO FILL THAT VOID IN THEIR HEARTS

244
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,600
THE INSTRUMENTALITY OF HEARTS
AND SOULS BEGINS

245
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:28,850
RETURNING ALL THINGS TO NOTHINGNESS

246
00:10:28,890 --> 00:10:31,020
THE INSTRUMENTALITY OF PEOPLE HAD BEGUN

247
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:35,200
No, it is not that we are returning
to nothingness.

248
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:38,040
We are only restoring everything
to its original state.

249
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:41,490
We are only returning to our mother,
who has been lost to this world.

250
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:45,320
All souls will become one
and find eternal peace.

251
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:48,210
That is all there is to it.

252
00:10:48,210 --> 00:10:49,750
And that's the Instrumentality Project?

253
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:50,880
That's right.

254
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:55,440
There is always a void, a part that
has been lost in our hearts.

255
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:56,760
THAT IS WHAT GIVES RISE TO THE
HUNGER IN OUR HEARTS

256
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,380
THIS IS WHAT GIVES RISE TO FEAR AND INSECURITY

257
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:01,660
Every single person fears that
darkness in their heart

258
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:05,340
and lives life trying to escape from it,
to banish it.

259
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:08,670
Even though it will never disappear
as long as we remain human.

260
00:11:08,670 --> 00:11:11,400
That's why you're going to bundle
all human souls together,

261
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:13,670
so we can compensate for
the void in each other?!

262
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:16,710
And you're just going to do this to everyone?!
Mind your own business!

263
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:19,240
That's nothing more than
a conspiracy to deceive us!

264
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,660
But you've been wishing for it to happen too.

265
00:11:23,930 --> 00:11:25,740
Where am I?

266
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:27,240
IN THE CASE OF MISATO KATSURAGI

267
00:11:27,830 --> 00:11:31,690
This is the me that exists
in your mind, Miss Misato.

268
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:35,880
And at the same time, the me
that exists in your mind, right?

269
00:11:36,210 --> 00:11:40,610
I must connect with all sorts of people
in order for me to find who I am.

270
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,880
I must search deep within myself.

271
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:46,640
I must search deep within the Miss Misato
that exists in my mind.

272
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:49,520
What is it that you want, Miss Misato?

273
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:50,730
"YOU WANT TO BE A GOOD GIRL?"

274
00:11:50,730 --> 00:11:53,140
I have to be a good girl.

275
00:11:53,190 --> 00:11:54,150
"WHY?"

276
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,750
Because my dad's not around.

277
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:59,420
I have to help my mom and be a good girl.

278
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:01,950
But I don't want to become like my mom,

279
00:12:01,950 --> 00:12:05,490
because she's always crying
when my dad isn't here.

280
00:12:05,490 --> 00:12:08,080
No crying, no being spoiled.

281
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:11,360
That's why I have to be a good girl.

282
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:14,610
And I'm going to do my best
so my dad won't hate me.

283
00:12:14,610 --> 00:12:16,800
But I hate my father.

284
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,940
That's why I hate being good too.

285
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:20,810
I hate it all now.

286
00:12:20,810 --> 00:12:22,440
And I'm so tired.

287
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,940
Of having to maintain my clean image.

288
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:27,760
Of myself, for keeping up this pretense
of being so pristine.

289
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:29,800
I'm just tired of it.

290
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:32,460
I want to be dirty.

291
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:35,290
I wanted to see what I looked like
when I was no longer perfect.

292
00:12:35,290 --> 00:12:37,690
Is that why you slept with him? With that man?

293
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:41,040
No, I slept with him because I loved him.

294
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:44,030
Did you really love him?

295
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:45,360
Yes, I did.

296
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:47,920
He accepted me for who I am.

297
00:12:47,950 --> 00:12:48,740
"REALLY?"

298
00:12:49,010 --> 00:12:50,240
He was kind to me!

299
00:13:02,670 --> 00:13:06,590
No! Stop it! Don't show this part of me to Shinji!

300
00:13:07,930 --> 00:13:10,560
There's no reason to be embarrassed
after all that has happened.

301
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:12,390
It IS embarrassing!

302
00:13:12,390 --> 00:13:14,090
Why is it embarrassing?

303
00:13:14,090 --> 00:13:17,630
You have no problem...
no, you actually enjoy

304
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:19,770
presenting this side of yourself
to the man you love.

305
00:13:19,770 --> 00:13:21,190
No! Please stop!

306
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:27,010
In all honesty, you are actually
happy to show this to Shinji.

307
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:29,540
That's a lie! You're wrong! Wrong!

308
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:31,010
I don't know about that.

309
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:33,780
You actually want to show this
to your father, don't you?

310
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,180
You're wrong!

311
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:38,880
You sought peace in Kaji's face as he slept.

312
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:39,820
You're wrong!

313
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:42,990
You sought peace in Kaji's warmth.

314
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:44,390
You're wrong!

315
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:47,880
You sought your father in Kaji's arms.

316
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:48,890
It's not true!

317
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:52,800
That's right.

318
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:57,250
That time, I saw my own father in Kaji.

319
00:13:57,780 --> 00:14:00,290
That's why I ran away from him.

320
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:03,310
I was scared.

321
00:14:03,310 --> 00:14:05,490
It was as if he were my father and...

322
00:14:05,990 --> 00:14:08,650
But it was actually because I was happy.

323
00:14:08,650 --> 00:14:10,800
I derived pleasure from it.

324
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:13,850
It was a moment of unbearably
wonderful feeling.

325
00:14:13,850 --> 00:14:15,950
That's why I hated it.

326
00:14:15,950 --> 00:14:18,060
That's why I split up with him.

327
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:21,830
Well, I guess it just means love
begins for no reason,

328
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:24,010
but always ends for a reason.

329
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:27,370
You're so kind, Kaji.

330
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:31,120
Please take that kindness...

331
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:34,510
...and tarnish me with it.

332
00:14:36,490 --> 00:14:39,010
Just because you hate yourself now

333
00:14:39,010 --> 00:14:41,050
doesn't mean you should hurt yourself.

334
00:14:41,050 --> 00:14:46,230
That's just fooling yourself into feeling better
by punishing yourself for the moment.

335
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:48,490
You should stop doing that.

336
00:14:48,490 --> 00:14:52,290
And you're going to tell me
to be good to myself, right?

337
00:14:52,290 --> 00:14:54,130
That's what all men are like.

338
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:58,380
And after that, they go off to work,
into their own worlds.

339
00:14:58,380 --> 00:15:00,380
Leaving me behind...

340
00:15:01,410 --> 00:15:03,680
Just like Father.

341
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:07,220
All I'm ever doing is running away
from the harsh reality.

342
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:09,170
Harsh reality?

343
00:15:09,170 --> 00:15:10,940
That's me, isn't it?

344
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:14,660
Of course, just look at me.
It's only to be expected.

345
00:15:16,230 --> 00:15:18,230
Stop it, Miss Misato!

346
00:15:18,930 --> 00:15:22,440
Sometimes, I lose all hope for myself!
I hate it!

347
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:24,920
Filth, you're so dirty.

348
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:26,020
You're pathetic.

349
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:28,230
Disgusting! You're just foul!

350
00:15:28,230 --> 00:15:31,070
That's what you call a mature relationship?!
You make me puke!

351
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:35,370
Congratulations on your promotion,
Major Katsuragi.

352
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:36,970
The person being recognized

353
00:15:36,970 --> 00:15:39,640
is the me who's putting on a performance
in order to be recognized.

354
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,290
It's not the real me.

355
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:45,110
The real you is always crying.

356
00:15:45,110 --> 00:15:47,730
No, I'm happy.

357
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:48,670
"AM I HAPPY?"

358
00:15:48,890 --> 00:15:50,870
I'm happy.

359
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:51,840
"AM I HAPPY?"

360
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,680
I am happy!

361
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,680
"AM I HAPPY?"

362
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:57,440
No! This isn't happiness!

363
00:15:57,470 --> 00:15:58,430
"WHAT IS HAPPINESS?"

364
00:15:58,430 --> 00:16:01,390
This isn't the real me!

365
00:16:01,390 --> 00:16:03,660
I've only made myself believe that it is!

366
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:06,690
Is that what we have to do to keep on living?

367
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:09,370
You're afraid when you're not together.

368
00:16:09,370 --> 00:16:10,770
You're insecure.

369
00:16:10,770 --> 00:16:12,940
Unless someone's sleeping by your side.

370
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:15,170
Are you scared of sleeping by yourself?

371
00:16:15,170 --> 00:16:18,010
Are you lonely sleeping by yourself after all?

372
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:20,430
You can't bear the loss in your heart.

373
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:22,960
That's why you'll be with anyone,
it doesn't matter who.

374
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,520
That's not true!

375
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:28,190
No, you just want to give yourself
over to simple pleasure.

376
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:31,490
You just want to soothe your soul
through temporary escapes

377
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:34,430
and you're only using men to that end.

378
00:16:34,430 --> 00:16:36,580
No! You're wrong! Wrong!

379
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:40,310
WHAT COULD IT BE THAT SHE WANTS?

380
00:16:41,850 --> 00:16:43,820
Where am I?

381
00:16:44,850 --> 00:16:47,710
This is the me that exists in your mind, Asuka.

382
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:51,820
Which means, it's also the me
that exists in your mind, right?

383
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,900
IN THE CASE OF ASUKA LANGLEY SOHRYU

384
00:16:54,390 --> 00:16:56,220
Asuka, what do you want?

385
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:59,420
I'm going to live on my own!

386
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:02,550
I don't need Mom or Dad.
I'm going to live by myself.

387
00:17:02,550 --> 00:17:04,640
I'm not going to cry anymore.

388
00:17:06,170 --> 00:17:08,210
But I'm still crying...

389
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:10,440
Why am I crying?

390
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:14,600
I don't know how to deal with that child.

391
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:17,640
What's this? You, a doctor, getting
discouraged? It isn't like you.

392
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:19,440
Even doctors are human,

393
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:21,220
as I have mentioned before.

394
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:25,510
But a woman like you having
trouble with a child...

395
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:27,280
She's oddly mature,

396
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:30,420
and there's a sense of vigilant
and absolute rejection.

397
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,580
It scares me sometimes.

398
00:17:32,580 --> 00:17:35,250
Haven't you ever felt that way, dear?

399
00:17:35,250 --> 00:17:36,720
No.

400
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:40,020
Anyway, you're Asuka's mother now.

401
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:43,860
But before that, I first became your wife.

402
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:45,100
You became both at the same time.

403
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:48,050
Yes, from a social standpoint, that's true.

404
00:17:48,580 --> 00:17:51,840
But you can never stop being that child's father,

405
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:55,650
whereas I can quit being her mother at any time.

406
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:57,340
True enough.

407
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:00,410
Don't, Mom! Don't quit being my mom!

408
00:18:00,410 --> 00:18:03,180
I'll be a good girl, so you'll like me!

409
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:05,390
So, don't quit being my mom!

410
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:07,420
So, look at me!

411
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:08,650
Stop, Mom!

412
00:18:08,650 --> 00:18:10,640
Don't kill me!

413
00:18:11,110 --> 00:18:15,710
Your dad doesn't love your mom anymore.
He doesn't need me.

414
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:19,320
No, he never loved me to begin with.

415
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:22,550
He probably didn't need me from the start.

416
00:18:22,850 --> 00:18:28,040
So, die with me, because your dad
doesn't need us.

417
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:30,990
Am I a bother? Am I not needed?

418
00:18:31,330 --> 00:18:33,670
Please die with me.

419
00:18:33,670 --> 00:18:37,160
No! I'm not your doll, Mom!

420
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,720
I'll think for myself and live on my own!

421
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:45,230
That time, my mom was hanging
from the ceiling.

422
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:49,100
The expression on her face
looked very happy.

423
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:53,480
But I hated that look on her face.

424
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:58,150
I don't want to die. I don't want to disappear.

425
00:18:58,150 --> 00:19:01,880
I hate boys. I hate Mom and Dad too!

426
00:19:02,190 --> 00:19:03,980
I hate everybody!

427
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:06,820
No one will protect me.

428
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:08,870
No one will stay with me.

429
00:19:08,910 --> 00:19:10,370
WHAT DOES SHE WANT?

430
00:19:11,130 --> 00:19:13,500
That's why I'm going to live by myself.

431
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:16,070
But I don't want to! It's hard!

432
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,290
I don't want to be alone!

433
00:19:18,290 --> 00:19:20,140
I don't want to be alone!

434
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:22,470
I don't want to be alone!

435
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:27,000
Don't forsake me.

436
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,470
Don't abandon me.

437
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:30,210
Don't kill me.

438
00:19:32,650 --> 00:19:33,860
What is this?

439
00:19:36,090 --> 00:19:40,410
The Human Instrumentality Project
that your father was working on.

440
00:19:40,410 --> 00:19:41,410
This is?

441
00:19:41,410 --> 00:19:43,250
It appears to be part of it.

442
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:46,500
Because the truth eludes even us.

443
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:51,160
Only what you can feel for yourself
right now is fact.

444
00:19:51,570 --> 00:19:53,240
Within you.

445
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:57,800
And your memory of those things
will become the truth for you.

446
00:19:58,180 --> 00:20:01,330
There are also some truths
that change with time.

447
00:20:01,330 --> 00:20:05,300
So, this is fact, the result of everything
that was done. This...

448
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:08,320
There are a lot of realities.
This is one of them.

449
00:20:08,690 --> 00:20:10,810
This is the result you wished for.

450
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:13,080
The one I wished for?

451
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:17,350
Yes, annihilation, a world
where no one is saved.

452
00:20:17,350 --> 00:20:21,400
No! It's just that no one saved me! No one...

453
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:23,820
No one can save you.

454
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:26,570
This is what you wished for.

455
00:20:26,570 --> 00:20:29,960
Destruction, death, the return to nothingness...

456
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:32,160
It's what you wished for.

457
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:34,070
This is reality.

458
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:35,930
What is reality?

459
00:20:35,930 --> 00:20:37,900
It's your world.

460
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:42,090
It's your own world where you coexist
with time, space, and other people.

461
00:20:42,490 --> 00:20:47,350
It's a world where you yourself decide
how to perceive and accept it.

462
00:20:47,350 --> 00:20:50,700
Right now, this is your world,
where everything is given to you.

463
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,850
THAT IS REALITY

464
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:54,600
This is your world, which cannot be helped.

465
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:58,120
It's a world where everything's already set!

466
00:20:58,120 --> 00:21:01,340
You're wrong. It's a world where
you make the decisions.

467
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:04,950
It's a world where your heart
has decided that it is so.

468
00:21:04,990 --> 00:21:06,110
THIS IS REALITY

469
00:21:06,110 --> 00:21:07,950
Your will to live...

470
00:21:07,950 --> 00:21:11,950
Your thoughts of wanting to die...
They are all what you wished for.

471
00:21:11,950 --> 00:21:15,040
You're saying even this darkness
and this world of half measures

472
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,280
are all things I wished for?

473
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,440
That's right.

474
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:22,760
You wished for a closed world,
where you alone are comfortable.

475
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:25,650
In order to protect the weakness of your heart.

476
00:21:25,650 --> 00:21:28,250
In order to protect your pleasures in life.

477
00:21:28,250 --> 00:21:30,430
This is merely the result.

478
00:21:30,430 --> 00:21:32,890
For people cannot live in a world
that is yours alone.

479
00:21:32,890 --> 00:21:35,530
They cannot live in a space
that is closed off.

480
00:21:35,530 --> 00:21:40,200
But you wished for the world, the world
that surrounds you, to be closed off.

481
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:43,870
Your heart and mind eliminated
everything you didn't like

482
00:21:43,870 --> 00:21:45,740
and wished for a world as solitary as possible.

483
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:49,920
And that has led to this little haven for your soul.

484
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:54,880
This is one of the many ends that could occur.

485
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:58,400
This is the end of the world
that you have brought about.

486
00:21:58,420 --> 00:21:59,960
AND THE JOURNEY TOWARDS INSTRUMENTALITY...

487
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:01,630
...WILL CONTINUE

488
00:23:07,070 --> 00:23:07,900
PREVIEW

489
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:11,690
The end, it is something that always
comes after the beginning.

490
00:23:11,690 --> 00:23:14,260
Will our wishes lead to destruction?

491
00:23:14,260 --> 00:23:16,860
Is our hope death itself?

492
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:20,890
Final episode: "The Beast That Shouted Love
at the Heart of the World"

493
00:23:18,910 --> 00:23:22,080
FINAL EPISODE

494
00:23:18,910 --> 00:23:22,080
THE BEAST THAT SHOUTED LOVE
AT THE HEART OF THE WORLD
